From f782c2b9d55372772f17063101bf75f661c28425 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: leo <leoschlosser@tutamail.com>
Date: Tue, 3 Nov 2026 01:12:30 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 116/117] media: i2c: s5c73m3: name the firmware file after any
 module letter

The firmware file for SPI booting is SlimISP_<maker><module>.bin, from
the first two letters of the firmware version in the module's F-ROM,
but only the module letters C to F were taken over: those of the
Galaxy S III. The Galaxy Note II's module reports GKFH93 and Samsung
ships SlimISP_GK.bin for it, yet the driver asked for SlimISP_GC.bin.

Take any upper-case letter.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 drivers/media/i2c/s5c73m3/s5c73m3-core.c | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/media/i2c/s5c73m3/s5c73m3-core.c b/drivers/media/i2c/s5c73m3/s5c73m3-core.c
index 551387cea..9de9ea9f3 100644
--- a/drivers/media/i2c/s5c73m3/s5c73m3-core.c
+++ b/drivers/media/i2c/s5c73m3/s5c73m3-core.c
@@ -647,7 +647,7 @@ static void s5c73m3_set_fw_file_version(struct s5c73m3 *state)
 	}
 
 	switch (state->sensor_fw[1]) {
-	case 'C'...'F':
+	case 'A'...'Z':
 		state->fw_file_version[1] = state->sensor_fw[1];
 		break;
 	}
-- 
